>As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and August to September, September to October and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 35 of 75 years. In 2025, the middle of the grids got 135% of normal in April to May and 52% in November to December. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 42% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 21518 had its driest year in 1965 at 65%.</p>"}
